From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yanan He <yanan.he@linux.dev>
Date: Thu, 4 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] alsactl: skip custom strlcpy/strlcat fallbacks on glibc >= 2.38

glibc 2.38 added strlcpy/strlcat to <string.h>, so the static fallback
definitions in init_sysdeps.c now conflict with the libc declarations
("static declaration of 'strlcpy' follows non-static declaration") and
break the build. Only compile the fallbacks when the libc is known to
lack the functions.

Upstream fixed this the same way in alsa-utils 1.2.8.

Upstream-Status: Backport [alsa-utils 1.2.8]
Signed-off-by: Yanan He <yanan.he@linux.dev>
---
 alsactl/init_sysdeps.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/alsactl/init_sysdeps.c b/alsactl/init_sysdeps.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/alsactl/init_sysdeps.c
+++ b/alsactl/init_sysdeps.c
@@ -18,7 +18,8 @@
  *
  */

-#if defined(__GLIBC__) && !(defined(__UCLIBC__) && defined(__USE_BSD))
+#if defined(__GLIBC__) && !(defined(__UCLIBC__) && defined(__USE_BSD)) && \
+	(__GLIBC__ < 2 || (__GLIBC__ == 2 && __GLIBC_MINOR__ < 38))
 static size_t strlcpy(char *dst, const char *src, size_t size)
 {
 	size_t bytes = 0;
--
2.34.1
